
# netsurf: name the cause of every batch full reconvert (patch 308)
# Generated 2026-10-19
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 307)
#
# Doc-20 stage 0. Instrumentation only -- zero behaviour change. The
# reconvert flush paths (macos9_reconvert_cb and the sync
# macos9_reconvert_flush_now) already know when a pending batch takes
# a full reconvert, but nothing records WHY; this patch counts the
# cause per navigation and prints it beside the INHERITEDCOLOR
# summary, so stage 1's bound is sized from data instead of from the
# bench pages' 18-mark show() bursts.
#
#   - macos9_reconvert_pending gains coarse_cause: 1 when a mark
#     names no node, 2 when more distinct marks arrive than the
#     extra ring holds (first cause wins; the slot already drops
#     its references on going coarse).
#   - macos9_reconvert_try_local names its own failure: kind (the
#     mutation kind has no local answer, doc-20 T4), local (the
#     local path declined, T6), two (two marks declined in
#     sequence, T5 -- the defer-and-retry found a second).
#     try_local_one classifies the single-mark decline; declines
#     stay non-destructive, the counting reads only.
#   - The flush sites count before clearing the slot, only when
#     html_reconvert_content is actually taken (rc == 0); the
#     busy/declined paths are not full reconverts and are not
#     counted. Initial conversions are never counted -- the
#     census is about batches, doc-20 T2-T7.
#   - The line reads, e.g.:
#     LIFE FULLCAUSE total=1 over=0 nonode=0 kind=0 local=0 two=1
#     and is printed per navigation from macos9_reconvert_sync_reset,
#     the same cadence as the other LIFE summaries.
#
# Overhead: one int per pending slot, six longs, one debug line per
# navigation that had a batch full reconvert. No hot path changes.
#
# Gate: run-one.sh on JS-dom-stall.html (page passes, no batch full
# reconverts -- the census correctly reports nothing), a throwaway
# forced-full page (40-mark burst -> over=1; setAttribute burst ->
# kind=1, page text correct after both full reconverts), and the
# full adapted gate with all structural counts held.
#
# First datum from the instrumented gate: the suite's own pages take
# batch full reconverts through two-in-sequence declines (two=1
# lines across the CSS pages) -- the structural-interaction class
# of patches 192/198 -- while over/nonode/kind stay 0 on the bench
# pages, as expected post-301.
#
# Perf: instrumentation only; no before/after claimed.
# No vitaSDK on this VM; the Vita cross-build does not run here.
